t would break All Simples. Since All Simples + No Honors gives at least 3 points (2+1), better to aim for that. Also, opponents may need terminals/honors; discarding W1 could be risky as it's a terminal. B4 appears safer: across player has B1-B3 and B7-B9 chows, so may not need B4; next player has not collected B tiles much; previous player discarded B2 and B7. So B4 seems relatively safe. Also, keeping W7 and W6 gives potential W6-W7-W8 chow if we draw W8 (only 1 left), but slim. T5 is central and useful for chows with T4 and T6. T6 we have two, good for pair or chow. B7 pair is good for final pair. So discard B4 to reduce isolated tile while maintaining flexibility.\n\nAnswer: Play B4"}
